exercises.instructions:
Write a function called `genreBreakdown` that takes an array of artist objects and returns an object where each key is a genre and the value is an object with:
- `artistCount`: number of artists in that genre
- `totalListeners`: sum of `monthlyListeners` for artists in that genre

Note: artists can have multiple genres, so they may appear in more than one entry.

Example:
```
genreBreakdown(artists)
// Returns: {
//   "pop": { artistCount: 3, totalListeners: 221000000 },
//   "hip-hop": { artistCount: 2, totalListeners: 129300000 },
//   ...
// }
```

exercises.solution:
function genreBreakdown(artists) {
  return artists.reduce((breakdown, artist) => {
    artist.genres.forEach(genre => {
      if (!breakdown[genre]) {
        breakdown[genre] = { artistCount: 0, totalListeners: 0 };
      }
      breakdown[genre].artistCount++;
      breakdown[genre].totalListeners += artist.monthlyListeners;
    });
    return breakdown;
  }, {});
}

