exercises.instructions:
Write a function called `labelPortfolio` that takes the `artists` and `albums` arrays and returns an object where each key is a label name and the value is an object with:
- `artists`: array of unique artist names signed to that label
- `albumCount`: total number of albums released on that label
- `totalSales`: sum of `certification.sales` for albums on that label

Labels appear in both `artist.labels[]` and `album.label` (use album.label for counting albums and sales).

Example:
```
labelPortfolio(artists, albums)
// Returns: {
//   "Rimas": { artists: ["Bad Bunion"], albumCount: 2, totalSales: 11700000 },
//   ...
// }
```

exercises.solution:
function labelPortfolio(artists, albums) {
  const portfolio = {};
  artists.forEach(artist => {
    artist.labels.forEach(label => {
      if (!portfolio[label]) portfolio[label] = { artists: [], albumCount: 0, totalSales: 0 };
      if (!portfolio[label].artists.includes(artist.name)) {
        portfolio[label].artists.push(artist.name);
      }
    });
  });
  albums.forEach(album => {
    if (!portfolio[album.label]) portfolio[album.label] = { artists: [], albumCount: 0, totalSales: 0 };
    portfolio[album.label].albumCount++;
    portfolio[album.label].totalSales += album.certification.sales;
  });
  return portfolio;
}

