exercises.instructions:
Write a function called `tallestPerFaction` that takes an array of character objects and returns an object where each key is a faction name and the value is `{ name, height }` of the tallest character in that faction.

Example:
```
tallestPerFaction(characters)
// Returns: { "Rebel Alliance": { name: "Chew-Tobacco", height: 2.28 }, ... }
```

exercises.starterCode:
/**
 * @param {Object[]} characters - Array of character objects
 * @returns {Object} Map of faction to { name, height } of tallest member
 */
function tallestPerFaction(characters) {

}

exercises.solution:
function tallestPerFaction(characters) {
  const result = {};
  characters.forEach(c => {
    if (!result[c.faction] || c.height > result[c.faction].height) {
      result[c.faction] = { name: c.name, height: c.height };
    }
  });
  return result;
}

